The Los Angeles Lakers &#x2019; $100 coffee-table book i s getting a five-figure upgrade.

Luxury art-book publisher Taschen and the Lakers have unveiled two limited-edition versions of "Lakers: An Official History of the Purple & Gold,&#x201D; featuring original handprints from Showtime-era legends, authenticated hardwood from the former Staples Center court and exclusive artwork signed by Magic Johnson and Kareem Abdul-Jabbar. Related Stories Netflix Names Mattel Executive Roberto Stanichi as VP of Consumer Products and Experiences Malaysian War Drama 'The Ghost and the Gun' Sets Global Netflix Release (EXCLUSIVE)

The new releases, announced Thursday, are limited to 1,100 copies worldwide, with 1,000 Collector&#x2019;s Editions priced at $2,400 each and just 100 Art Editions retailing for $9,600. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Both versions include the original 528-page book, housed in a custom leather clamshell box designed by Jeff Hamilton, the fashion designer known for his elaborate leather jackets commemorating the Lakers&#x2019; championship victories in 2000, 2001, 2002 and 2020.

Each box also contains an authenticated piece of hardwood from the original Staples Center floor, where the Lakers won five championships and Kobe Bryant played his final NBA game. Collectors will receive an original handprint from one of seven Showtime-era figures &#x2014; Johnson, Abdul-Jabbar, James Worthy, Michael Cooper, Kurt Rambis, Byron Scott or Pat Riley &#x2014; with the identity revealed upon delivery.

The $9,600 Art Edition takes things a step further, adding a large-format print of Ernie Barnes&#x2019; &#x201C;Fastbreak,&#x201D; originally commissioned by the Lakers in 1987. The 41-by-24.5-inch artwork depicts the team in the midst of its Showtime era and features seven signature plates hand-signed by the players and coach portrayed in the painting. Each print is numbered and authenticated by the Estate of Ernie Barnes. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The limited editions arrive nearly two months after Taschen released the standard version of the book in September. Abdul-Jabbar wrote the foreword, Lakers governor Jeanie Buss contributed the introduction and former coach Phil Jackson penned the afterword. Other contributors include Johnson, O&#x2019;Neal, Pau Gasol, LeBron James, Luka Don&#x10D;i&#x107;, Jack Nicholson, Paula Abdul, Flea and Lou Adler.

&#x201C;The Lakers have had an extraordinary impact on basketball and pop culture, and we wanted this book to capture the full scope of that influence, from the game itself to art, fashion, music, and beyond,&#x201D; Tobak said in a statement. &#x201C;The Limited Edition takes that vision a step further, bringing together rare memorabilia, artwork, and personal contributions from the people who helped shape the team&#x2019;s history.&#x201D;

Both limited editions are available now through Taschen&#x2019;s website.

More than 20 years later, The Family Stone sequel has become a real-life family reunion of sorts for the cast of the 2005 holiday movie.

Dermot Mulroney , who reprises his role as Everett Stone in the upcoming sequel The Families Stone , recently expressed that he's "so moved to be reunited" with his "incredible, incredible" co-stars from the original Thomas Bezucha-written/directed film.

"Everybody's had this remarkable career advancement and paths since we were all together," he told Entertainment Weekly . "So we're making a movie about a family returning all together for the first time in years and years, and we're doing that in real life too, returning and reuniting with this incredible cast." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

